---
alwaysApply: true
---

When using, updating ui components, or building interfaces using ui components, follow the following rules:

- always use the shadcn mcp tools
- prefer using existing components in galipette-portal/common/components or galipette-portal/common/ui if they already exists
- you may create variant of component for specific needs
- when searching for component using the mcp tools, start by checking the registeries, then the demo of these components
- if ts errors arise, fix them
- ensure the color used derives from user theme

When building complex interface, check if a block is available.
You may create/add features to existing block => ensure it follow SOLID principles and doesn't brek current implementation

You should prefer the composition of existing UI component / blocks, instead of defining custom DOM elements or CSS

The goal is to factorize as much code aspossible
